<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</title>
<headline>Brazil Paranagua/Santos sugar shipping conditions.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Santos reported the following conditions for shipping sugar.</p>
<p>PARANAGUA:</p>
<p>Vessels: (On June 5) Karyatis III loading 25,000 tonnes using big bags. Ailsa loading 25,000 tonnes bulk sugar. Lucky Way loading 14,000 tonnes using big bags. Waiting to dock, eight vessels to load using big bags and one bulk.</p>
<p>Road: no figures available.</p>
<p>Loading: no figures available.</p>
<p>Stocks: no figures available.</p>
<p>SANTOS:</p>
<p>Vessels: Araya loading 35,200 tonnes bulk sugar, Cormorant loading 14,000 tonnes bagged sugar, Unisea loading 14,000 tonnes bagged sugar, Qing Jiang loading 14,000 bagged sugar. Waiting to dock, six vessels to load bagged sugar and four to load bulk.</p>
<p>Stocks: 42,500 tonnes bulk in CODESP warehouses, no bagged sugar. Private warehouses already with bagged sugar but stock levels unavailable.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
